Evaluator access
================

The claims that matter for the Reproducible badge (1, 2, 3, 5) need no access to
author hardware. They run from the shipped logs on a stock Python environment.

Claim 4 in scaled mode needs only a Docker host and an API key for one hosted
model. Evaluators who prefer not to use their own credentials, or who want the
full-scale GPU configuration, may request temporary access to author hardware
through the HotCRP thread for this submission. We will supply an SSH endpoint,
a scoped account, and a time-boxed API key for the evaluation period.

We commit to being reachable through HotCRP for the whole evaluation window,
including the kick-the-tires period.
